  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds one ground plane and 10,000 instanced objects as three nodes: 8,000 cylinder trunks, 8,000 cone canopies and 2,000 sphere rocks. Positions come from a seeded mulberry32 RNG, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours on white base materials. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, fitted explicitly to the forest. It also has a hemisphere fill light and `effects.fog` with mode \"exp\" (exponential). The camera orbits at radius 112 and height 76, about one lap in 52 s, with the whole forest in view. I move it each frame with `app.camera?.setPose`. `__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`. I avoided top-level await because there is no vite.config.ts, and Vite's default build target may reject it. Typecheck passes. I could not run `vite build` or view a render, so the shadow fit, fog density, camera framing and whether `setPose` moves the scene camera are unchecked by a render.",
